<header><p class="st-kicker">county · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Earldom of Desmond</h1><p class="st-meta">1329 CE – 1583 CE · capital Askeaton</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The FitzGerald lordship of Munster that became more Gaelic than the Gaels, destroyed in the Desmond Rebellions of the 1570s and 1580s.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fitzgerald-dynasty">FitzGeralds</a> descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurice-fitzgerald-lord-of-lanstephan">Maurice FitzGerald</a>, one of the first Cambro-Norman invaders of 1169. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurice-fitzthomas-fitzgerald-1st-earl-of-desmond">Maurice FitzThomas FitzGerald</a> was created Earl of Desmond in 1329 with palatine rights over <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ciarraige-luachra">Kerry</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Desmond earls ruled much of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-munster">Munster</a> from castles such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/askeaton">Askeaton</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newcastle-west">Newcastle West</a>, adopting Irish language, law and patronage of poets. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerald-fitzgerald-3rd-earl-of-desmond">Gerald, the 3rd Earl</a>, was a noted Irish poet. They were often at odds with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/butler-dynasty">Butler</a> earls of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/earldom-of-ormond">Earldom of Ormond</a> and with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerald-fitzgerald-14th-earl-of-desmond">Gerald FitzGerald</a>, the 15th Earl, rebelled against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/desmond-rebellions">Desmond Rebellions</a>. He was killed in 1583, and his vast lands were confiscated and granted to English settlers in the Plantation of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-munster">Munster</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/earldom-of-desmond.jpg" alt="Earldom of Desmond" width="320" height="352"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blason_famille_ie_Fitzgerald_de_Desmond.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1329 CE – 1583 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Askeaton</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Maurice FitzThomas FitzGerald, Gerald FitzGerald, 3rd Earl of Desmond, Gerald FitzGerald, 15th Earl of Desmond</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Irish, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Palatinate of Kerry, Desmond FitzGeralds</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1456&amp;focus=earldom-of-desmond" aria-label="Earldom of Desmond on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4479 364 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Earldom of Desmond lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4799 620L4861 599M4799 620L4861 599"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4861 599h0M4861 599h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4799 620h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4799 620h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Askeaton. <a href="/atlas?year=1456&amp;focus=earldom-of-desmond">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

